          "emails": null,
          "description": "We are seeking a **Project Manager** to lead a large cross-functional team of developers and testers in a strategic project for a corporate client in the telecommunications sector. This is a fixed-price initiative under an agile framework (hybrid approach) focused on the construction and reengineering of components for various modules of a business-critical system. The core stack includes Oracle (PL/SQL, Forms), Java, and React. This role is key to upholding commitments, protecting the agreed scope, and ensuring the project's profitability.\n\n**Responsibilities**\n\n* Define, monitor, and protect the scope baseline, ensuring that every deliverable meets commitments regarding schedule, cost, and quality\n* Plan realistic commitments with the client and the team, monitor progress, and flag risks early when deliverables are at risk, proposing alternatives and action plans\n* Manage budget, resource capacity, and profitability, accounting for leaves, freezes, and external dependencies\n* Standardize the estimation and story-based billing framework using objective criteria, reference stories, and clear rules to minimize subjectivity and client friction\n* Ensure user stories enter development fully refined, sized, and backed by agreed-upon acceptance criteria\n* Oversee the acceptance lifecycle: define the Definition of \"Done\" (DoD) with the client, track approval timelines, and facilitate the timely closure of each story to protect billing and cash flow\n* Recalibrate periodically actual effort against agreed sizing and data-driven adjustments\n* Manage the formal Change Request (CR) process: identify impacts on scope, schedule, and cost, and negotiate client approval, replacement, or renegotiation\n* Detect and manage scope creep during grooming/refinement, and negotiate changes and reprioritization using data and evidence, preserving trust and contractual boundaries\n* Identify, log, and proactively track technical, dependency, capacity, sign-off, and UAT acceptance risks, and define mitigation and contingency plans\n* Lead and organize the team, establishing technical and QA leadership, clear phase-gate processes, and shared quality ownership between development and testing\n* Facilitate Scrum ceremonies (Planning, Daily, Refinement, Sprint Review/Demo, and Retrospective) and manage the backlog alongside the client, prioritizing by value delivery or MVPs\n\n**Requirements**\n\n* Minimum of 5 years of experience leading software projects, with at least 3 years managing teams of 10 or more members\n* Proven experience in fixed-price projects, including scope, change, risk, and profitability management\n* Background in milestone- or story-based estimation and billing models, as well as sizing techniques (t-shirt sizing, story points, function points, or similar)\n* Solid background as a Scrum Master or facilitating Scrum ceremonies within large-scale teams\n* Track record of working with complex and demanding corporate clients, backed by strong negotiation skills\n* Proficiency in Jira and delivery metrics\n\n**We offer**\n\n* International projects with top brands\n* Work with global teams of highly skilled, diverse peers\n* Healthcare benefits\n* Employee financial programs\n* Paid time off and sick leave\n* Upskilling, reskilling and certification courses\n* Unlimited access to the LinkedIn Learning library and 22,000+ courses\n* Global career opportunities\n* Volunteer and community involvement opportunities\n* EPAM Employee Groups\n* Award-winning culture recognized by Glassdoor, Newsweek and LinkedIn",
