          "emails": null,
          "description": "### **SAP BTP Full Stack Developer**\n\n### **About the role**\n\nAs an **SAP BTP Full Stack Developer**, you will make an impact by designing and developing cloud-native solutions on SAP Business Technology Platform, extending SAP S/4HANA while supporting a clean-core architecture.\n\nYou will be a valued member of the **SAP Trulive project team**, collaborating with developers, architects, functional consultants, and business stakeholders to deliver document-processing solutions using **SAP Document AI, CAP, RAP, React, and TypeScript**.\n\n### **In this role, you will**\n\n* Design and develop full-stack applications on **SAP Business Technology Platform** using CAP, TypeScript, React, and SAP HANA Cloud.\n* Build CDS data models, APIs, service handlers, validations, and integrations with SAP Document AI and SAP S/4HANA.\n* Develop responsive user interfaces for document upload, data review, correction, approval, and status tracking.\n* Create and integrate RAP-based business objects and OData V4 services, following SAP clean-core and ABAP Cloud principles.\n* Configure application security, authentication, destinations, deployment, testing, monitoring, and CI/CD processes.\n\n### **Work model**\n\nWe believe hybrid work is the way forward as we strive to provide flexibility wherever possible.\n\nBased on this role’s business requirements, this is a **hybrid position requiring 2 days per week in a Cognizant or client office and 3 days working from home**.\n\nRegardless of your working arrangement, we are here to support a healthy work-life balance through our various wellbeing programs.\n\nThe working arrangements for this role are accurate as of the date of posting. This may change based on the project you are engaged in, as well as business and client requirements. Rest assured, we will always be clear about role expectations.\n\n### **What you need to have to be considered**\n\n* **5+ years of overall SAP development experience, including at least 3 years of hands-on experience with SAP BTP.**\n* Hands-on experience with **SAP CAP**, including CDS modeling, service development, event handlers, and OData or REST APIs.\n* Strong experience with **TypeScript and React** for full-stack application development.\n* Experience integrating SAP applications and services through APIs, destinations, authentication, and authorization.\n* Experience with **SAP HANA Cloud** and cloud-native application development.\n* Understanding of **SAP clean-core principles**.\n* Experience with RAP, ABAP Cloud, or SAP S/4HANA integrations.\n* Experience using Git and working with CI/CD and application deployment processes.\n\n### **These will help you stand out**\n\n* Experience implementing **SAP Document AI or Document Information Extraction** solutions.\n* Knowledge of RAP business objects, behavior definitions, draft handling, and OData V4 services.\n* Experience with XSUAA, SAP Cloud Identity Services, role collections, Cloud Connector, and MTA deployment.\n* Familiarity with SAP Business Application Studio and ABAP Development Tools.\n* Experience with testing tools such as Jest, Mocha, Vitest, React Testing Library, or ABAP Unit.\n* Knowledge of SAP Integration Suite, Event Mesh, or SAP Build solutions.\n\nWe're excited to meet people who share our mission and can make an impact in a variety of ways. Don't hesitate to apply, even if you only meet the minimum requirements listed. Think about your transferable experiences and unique skills that make you stand out as someone who can bring new and exciting things to this role.",
